WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
Checkout gets slow but keeps returning 200. The SLO alert catches it, traces point to the cause, and a fallback restores service.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Architecture: Telemetry flow.

3
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Architecture: Incident response sequence.

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Baseline: steady traffic, no requests slower than 300 ms, burn rate 0x.

5
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Fault injected in the inventory dependency. More than half of the requests miss the 300 ms objective and the burn rate passes the 14.4x paging threshold.

6
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Slow-request span timings show inventory.lookup taking about 800 ms while payment and persistence stay normal.

7
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The inventory cache fallback is enabled and the burn rate drops back to 0x.

8
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Detected, diagnosed, mitigated and recovered.

9
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Verified result. Source, tests and setup steps are linked below.
